# Version-Disabled Screens

These workspaces are shipped in code but must stay unreachable for every user and every subscription package until a later version re-enables them.

## Disabled destinations

Emergency, Rooms & beds, Physiotherapy, Operations, Housekeeping, Biomedical Engineering, Mortuary, Communications, Integrations.

## Permission domains (hard deny)

`emergency`, `rooms_beds`, `physiotherapy`, `operations`, `housekeeping`, `biomed`, `mortuary`, `communications`, `integration`.

## Enforcement

- Strip these domains from effective access on API and UI (including elevated roles).
- Omit them from all `PLAN_PERMISSION_CAPS` / `PlanPermissionCaps` tiers.
- Menu items and routes stay permission-gated; denied keys must hide shell destinations.
- Do not re-grant via role packs, custom plans, module entitlements, or direct user grants.
- To re-enable: remove the domain from `version-disabled-permissions` (BE + FE), restore plan caps, then drop this rule.

